  "createdAt": "2026-10-21T04:06:28.072Z",
  "summary": "The frozen wall-clock column in metrics-armA-v3.json / metrics-armB-v3.json was not measured on the v3 runs. It was copied verbatim from the earlier v2 batch by aggregate.mjs, which back-fills wall clock from runner logs and lets later logs win; the v3 logs contain no [done] lines. The +38.5% / p=0.032 wall-clock claim in the published report is therefore retracted. The true paired difference is +3.00s (+4.5%), p=0.684, not significant.",
  "rootCause": {
    "file": "work_space2/ab-v04/aggregate.mjs",
    "mechanism": "aggregate.mjs re-derives every numeric metric from events/*.jsonl, but wall clock is not in the event stream. It harvests wall from runner logs with /\\[done \\]\\s+(I\\d\\d-arm[AB])\\s+exit=\\d+\\s+calls=\\d+\\s+billed=\\d+\\s+bytes=\\d+\\s+wall=([\\d.]+)s/ and sorts logs by mtime so \"later logs win\". runA-v3.log / runB-v3.log contain zero [done] lines, so the v2 values survived.",
    "generalLesson": "Any metric aggregated across batches must be keyed by sessionId, never by a reusable run label such as I01-armB: the label collides across batches and silently splices one batch metric onto another batch row."
  },
